# Keep `git archive` output installable as-is.
#
# An Omeka S module is installed by unpacking a zip into `modules/`, so the
# archive should carry only what the module needs at runtime: Module.php,
# config/, src/, view/, asset/, language/. Everything below is development
# tooling — the Python generators run in CI (issue #7), never on the server.
#
# Deliberately no `text`/`eol` attributes here: this repo has never had a
# .gitattributes, and adding `* text=auto` now would renormalise every
# tracked file in one commit.

.github/            export-ignore
scripts/            export-ignore
tests/              export-ignore
.gitattributes      export-ignore
.gitignore          export-ignore
playwright.config.js export-ignore
package.json        export-ignore
package-lock.json   export-ignore
tokens.json         export-ignore
CLAUDE.md           export-ignore
REFACTORING.md      export-ignore
ROADMAP.md          export-ignore

# The Impeccable artifact layer: the design-system record, the product
# context it is written against, and the machine-readable sidecar the design
# detector reads. All three describe how to CHANGE this module in step with
# the IWAC theme — the same audience as CLAUDE.md above, and no part of what
# Omeka loads. They shipped inside every release archive up to and including
# v1.57.0 (81 KB of it) because the rule was never written down.
#
# They travel together on purpose. DESIGN.md's provenance comment and
# .impeccable/design.json are two halves of one record — the sidecar exists
# so the detector can read the palette the prose describes — so shipping
# either without the other would be worse than shipping both.
DESIGN.md           export-ignore
PRODUCT.md          export-ignore
.impeccable/        export-ignore
